<title>USA: Barry's Jewelers sees Q1 charge.</title>
<headline>Barry's Jewelers sees Q1 charge.</headline>
<dateline>MONROVIA, Calif. 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barry's Jewelers Inc said Thursday it expects to report an extraordinary pre-tax charge of about $876,000 against results for its first quarter ended August 31 related to the termination of agreements with Capital Markets Assurance Corp.</p>
<p>Barry's said it recently secured an $85 million revolving line of credit with First National Bank of Boston, a portion of which was used to retire outstanding obligations under a securitization facility with Capital Markets.</p>
<p>Barry's operates 171 retail jewelry stores in 17 states.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
